{
  "slug": "pmm",
  "name": "Pmm",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "If you have ever had AI hallucinate and make things up (and  gaslight you, even): it's because summaries do not preserve nuance.\n\nEach /compact cycle summarises and compresses. Decisions lose their rationale. Lessons lose their context. By Monday, you're re-explaining choices you made on Thursday. That's context rot.\n\nPMM fixes that. Every session, Claude loads what it already knows, then adds to it.\n\nMarkdown files, git-backed. No database, no setup. Decisions tracked with rationale: not just what but. git log as your memory audit trail.\n\nMemory that compounds, not rots.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **12 skills** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (12): `dump` (Dump PMM memory state as ASCII art in the terminal), `hydrate` (Populate empty or thin memory files from current session context), `init` (Initialize Poor Man's Memory in your project — runs preference wizard, scaffolds memory/ directory, configures hooks), `init-local-skills` (Install local skill variants for Cowork compatibility), `onboard` (Seed your user identity layer from a prior AI or direct interview), `query` (Query memory — context-first recall with deep traversal across vectors, graph, and taxonomy when needed), `recall` (Context-switching recall — synthesizes a focused briefing on a topic from across all memory files), `save` (Save current session to memory — dispatches maintain agent, updates memory files, commits to git), and 4 more\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install pmm@claude-community` from `NominexHQ/pmm-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 12,
    "hook": 2
  },
